{
  "description": "Planted-exposure set (spec 11). Each case is scanned with the frozen data in data/.",
  "data": {
    "archive_day": "2026-11-13",
    "oebc_generated": "2026-06-14",
    "osv_as_of": "2026-11-13"
  },
  "scan_args": [
    "--as-of",
    "2026-11-13",
    "--max-age-days",
    "200"
  ],
  "scan_args_why": "Ruling F: the frozen OEBC is the 2026-06-14 build and OSV the 2026-11-13 export. --as-of pins 'now' to the archive day and --max-age-days 200 covers the OEBC's age, so verdicts reflect grading, not staleness (with defaults every case would be DENY data_stale).",
  "selection": "Versions were chosen programmatically from the frozen records: for KEV cases the highest final release (within the named line) matched by a KEV-listed CVE whose tier is CRITICAL in the frozen OEBC; for HIGH/LOW the highest final release whose findings are all graded with that worst tier; benign bumps go to the fixed version, which has no advisories. scripts/freeze_fixtures.py re-checks every expected finding against the frozen data.",
